s -1, so a positive signed estimate would have meant stronger WRN dependency. The observed signed estimate is negative, -0.0330 [-0.0644, -0.0015], corresponding to the opposite raw direction: MYC-amplified lines are weakly associated with less negative WRN dependency, i.e. weaker WRN dependency. Although the interval excludes zero in the opposite direction, the magnitude is small, well below the practical benchmark, and arises after many exploratory comparisons. I reject the proposed claim and do not regard this as a scientifically meaningful new effect. I do not request validation for it because it is not meaningful in the claimed direction and would not change the substantive conclusion set.\n\nOverall, the evidence supports a focused set of dataset-level associations: TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency. The new nulls strengthen specificity. No validation is requested.",
