s specific reciprocal/gene-loss dependency relationships rather than broad driver-genotype or receptor-amplification genotype associations. Negative findings are substantial: canonical KRAS-mutation/BRAF-dependency, BRAF-V600E/BRAF-dependency, EGFR-amplification/EGFR-dependency, ERBB2-amplification/ERBB2-dependency, NF1-loss/dependency probes, MYC-amplification cross-pathway probes, many cross-pathway probes involving TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4/PTEN, and constructed marker assays were mostly near-null or rejected. The arbitrary research markers D/E/F and marker-interaction tests are now mostly null, reducing concern that the accepted associations are marker artifacts. Remaining unresolved uncertainty is mostly contextual or small-magnitude: H100 (CDKN2A-MDM2 within TP53-loss overall) and H160 (MTAP co-loss within CDKN2A-loss) have wide or nonconfirmatory intervals, and H170 (MYC-amplification-specific CDKN2A-MDM2) remains unresolved despite the validated MYC-mRNA-high context. Because no new validation requests remain and the key pending validation has arrived, the most informative next step is to close the remaining deferred specificity/generalizability panel using registered claims only. I activated H45, H46, H49, and H72 to test SMARCA2, WRN, and NFE2L2 main associations in Avana versus non-Avana library strata; H60, H61, and H62 to test whether TP53-USP7, SMARCA4-SMARCA2, and MSI-WRN associations are modified by sex, adherent culture status, or high serum media; and H89, H90, H142, H143, and H145 to finish useful driver/cross-pathway and SWI/SNF co-alteration probes. All conclusions remain associations within the supplied lung cell-line dataset, not causal claims or externally generalizable effects.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after synthesize iteration 13. No new validation requests remain. Accepted/validation updates: H150 now accepted/closed using R130+R142; CDKN2A-MDM2 stronger dependency is validated in TP53-loss MTAP-wildtype lines (validation +0.146, CI +0.023 to +0.269). H173 now accepted/closed using R163+R168; CDKN2A-MDM2 stronger dependency is validated in MYC mRNA upper-quartile lines (discovery +0.113, validation +0.172; validation CI +0.065 to +0.279). H170 remains unresolved/closed because validation R155 direction is positive but interval crosses zero; MYC expression context is better resolved than MYC amplification context. Current core accepted dataset-specific associations: TP53 loss weaker USP7 dependency (H7, H106, etc.); KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H13); SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H10 and contexts); MSI-high stronger WRN dependency (H8 and contexts); PTEN loss stronger STAT3 dependency (H67 and contexts); CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2 dependency overall (H94), in TP53-loss MTAP-wt (H150), and in MYC mRNA-high (H173). Negative/null: canonical driver genotype probes mostly null; marker D/E/F direct/interaction tests mostly null; many cross-pathway nulls; median MYC interactions for CDKN2A-MDM2 and PTEN-STAT3 null; ARID1A co-loss within SMARCA4-loss null. Unresolved: H100 TP53-loss overall CDKN2A-MDM2, H160 MTAP within CDKN2A-loss, H170 MYC-amplification-specific CDKN2A-MDM2, and several deferred context probes. Next active panel: H45, H46, H49, H72 for library-stratum direct effects; H60, H61, H62 for sex/culture/media interactions; H89, H90, H142, H143, H145 for remaining driver/cross-pathway/SWI/SNF probes. Do not interpret findings as causal or externally generalizable."
