  "narrative": "All 12 newly delivered comparisons are valid Welch tests with at least 20 observations in every comparison cell. Because estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, positive signed values support the claim. All 12 estimates are positive and their 95% intervals exclude zero. \n\nFor the strongest core associations, growth-rate stratification does not attenuate the effects. USP7 dependency versus TP53 loss is +0.807 in fast-growing lines and +0.814 in slow-growing lines. NFE2L2 dependency versus KEAP1 loss is +0.814 in fast-growing lines and +0.779 in slow-growing lines. SMARCA2 dependency versus SMARCA4 loss is +0.759 in fast-growing lines and +0.804 in slow-growing lines. WRN dependency versus MSI-high is +0.776 in fast-growing lines and +0.822 in slow-growing lines. These estimates are extremely large relative to the corresponding dependency-score distributions and far exceed any plausible 10% relative clinical threshold on the comparator scale. I accept H186-H189, H190-H193, and close these growth-stratified refinements.\n\nSTAT3 dependency versus PTEN loss remains robust across proliferation strata: +0.287 in fast-growing lines and +0.271 in slow-growing lines, with intervals excluding zero. These are not as enormous as the gene-loss effects, but they are substantial relative to STAT3 dependency variation and clearly support the accepted parent association in both strata. I accept H194-H195.\n\nCDKN2A loss versus MDM2 dependency is also positive in both growth strata: +0.090 in fast-growing lines and +0.136 in slow-growing lines. The fast-growth estimate is the smallest of the panel and should be read with more caution because its lower bound is closer to zero, but the interval excludes zero, the magnitude is large relative to comparator MDM2 dependency values and the prior overall CDKN2A-MDM2 association was independently validated. I accept H196-H197 as dataset-specific context-robust refinements, while noting that H196 is the most borderline for practical importance.\n\nThese results support robustness to measured proliferation, but they are still conditional associations within the supplied lung cell-line dataset. Stratifying by growth rate can reduce confounding by proliferation, but it can also condition on a variable related to screen dynamics and cellular state; it does not establish causality or external generalizability. Multiplicity remains a concern because these are 12 additional conditional tests. However, for USP7, NFE2L2, SMARCA2, WRN, STAT3, and overall MDM2, the parents were already accepted with large effects and several independent validations, making these new conditional results more credible than isolated subgroup artifacts. I request no validation because no voluntary validation budget remains.\n\nI also correct two historical near-null MTAP co-loss claims. H160 tested MTAP loss among CDKN2A-loss lines and had estimate +0.064 with interval including zero; H185 tested MTAP loss among CDKN2A-loss/TP53-wildtype lines and had estimate +0.065 with interval including zero. Neither provides evidence of a meaningful incremental MDM2-dependency effect beyond CDKN2A loss, so I assess both as reject and closed.",
