  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypotheses, so positive values support the claimed direction. The low-Cas9-activity stratum preserves every prespecified main effect: TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency (+0.812 [0.782, 0.842]), KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (+0.795 [0.763, 0.826]), SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (+0.774 [0.744, 0.804]), MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency (+0.815 [0.771, 0.858]), PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency (+0.278 [0.199, 0.356]), and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency (+0.084 [0.034, 0.135]). The first five are enormously larger than the 10% practical threshold; CDKN2A-MDM2 is smaller but its lower bound remains above an approximately 10% comparator-scale threshold and its CI excludes zero. These are dataset-specific robustness associations, not causal effects or evidence that Cas9 activity mediates the effects.\n\nThe lower-screen-ROC stratum (screen_roc_auc <= 0.9299) similarly preserves the four largest associations: USP7/TP53 loss (+0.782 [0.741, 0.824]), WRN/MSI-high (+0.780 [0.708, 0.852], despite only 28 exposed lines), STAT3/PTEN loss (+0.328 [0.226, 0.431]), and NFE2L2/KEAP1 loss (+0.793 [0.754, 0.832]). The CDKN2A-MDM2 estimate attenuates to +0.071 [0.006, 0.136]. Its direction is positive and statistically distinguishable at nominal alpha, but the lower bound is below an approximately 10% practical threshold, and adjusted/multiplicity-aware uncertainty would make even zero exclusion less compelling. Therefore H219 remains unresolved and is closed rather than accepted. This does not overturn the parent MDM2 association; it indicates possible attenuation in poorer-quality screens or insufficient precision in that subset. Small exposed cell sizes, especially for WRN/MSI-high, are a caution but meet the 20-cell rule.\n\nH221 does not revive the MYC-amplification/KIF18A hypothesis in the high-proliferation context. The signed estimate is -0.014 [-0.048, 0.021], i.e. a small effect in the opposite direction with an interval spanning null. The result is clinically and practically null, so I reject it. Overall multiplicity is nontrivial across these 12 exploratory robustness/context tests, but they were registered as prespecified follow-ups to accepted parents, several effects are massive, and only the already modest MDM2-low-ROC claim was ambiguous. I registered a new PTEN-loss and TP53-loss main-effect panel for the remaining largely unexplained dependencies as specificity mapping; these are non-directional exploratory tests that should only be accepted if intervals exclude both zero and the 10% practical threshold. No validation can be requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 17 appraise. Low-Cas9 robustness panel H210-H215 accepted: USP7-TP53 loss +0.812, NFE2L2-KEAP1 loss +0.795, SMARCA2-SMARCA4 loss +0.774, WRN-MSI-high +0.815, STAT3-PTEN loss +0.278, MDM2-CDKN2A loss +0.084 (lower bound ~0.034, practically meaningful). Low-screen-ROC panel H216-H220 accepted for USP7, WRN, STAT3, NFE2L2; H219 MDM2-CDKN2A unresolved/closed because +0.071 [0.006, 0.136] is too imprecise to establish a 10% practical difference. H221 high-proliferation MYC-KIF18A rejected (+/- signed estimate -0.014 [-0.048, 0.021]). Main accepted dataset associations remain: TP53 loss weaker USP7, KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2, SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high stronger WRN, PTEN loss stronger STAT3, CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2. Validation budget is exhausted. Registered new exploratory TP53-loss panel for BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, KRAS, RIT1, TMED10 and PTEN-loss specificity panel for RPL11, TMED10, KRAS, BRAF, ERBB2, DHX9, all direction -1 (stronger dependency) with anticipated direction 0. These map whether accepted effects are marker-specific and whether common tumor-suppressor losses explain unexplained dependencies. Next analysis should also consider useful deferred specificity/context tests and residual predictors, while treating all findings as dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims. MSI-high remains confounded with high TMB; low-TMB MSI is untestable."
