  "narrative": "No response deadlines or newly released validation comparisons are due in this synthesis, and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. Therefore this synthesis integrates the supplied discovery ledger and the validation evidence already recorded, without treating discovery intervals as validation. Using the supplied 10-percent practical yardstick as a context-specific benchmark for dependency-score differences, six marker-dependency associations are supported in this dataset and are the main scientifically meaningful findings. First, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: discovery R7 signed +0.802 [0.782,0.822], validation R92 +0.790 [0.761,0.819]; because more negative dependency scores indicate stronger dependency, the positive signed estimates mean TP53-loss lines are less negative, i.e. less dependent on USP7. Second, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency: accepted reversed claim H13 supported by R9 signed +0.796 [0.776,0.816] and validated by R26 +0.806 [0.775,0.838]. Third, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H10 supported by R10 signed +0.784 [0.765,0.803] and validated by R39 +0.793 [0.763,0.822]. Fourth, MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency: H8 supported by R8 signed +0.790 [0.760,0.819] and validated by R52 +0.802 [0.753,0.851]. Fifth, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency: H67 supported by R55 +0.267 [0.215,0.319] and validated by R65 +0.329 [0.255,0.402]; Avana-library robustness is supported by H245 R237 +0.288 [0.232,0.343]. Sixth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H94 supported by R62 +0.117 [0.082,0.152] and validated by R78 +0.130 [0.075,0.185]. The MDM2 effect is smaller than the four largest marker effects but is practically meaningful on the dependency-score scale and is repeatedly supported in demanding contexts: TP53-loss high-quality screens H234 R229 +0.132 [0.045,0.218], TP53-loss/MTAP-negative high-quality screens H253 R230 +0.122 [0.030,0.215], MYC-amplified high-quality screens H235 R231 +0.151 [0.044,0.258], and high-MYC-expression high-quality screens H254 R232 +0.133 [0.052,0.214]. These results argue that earlier uncertainty in TP53-loss and MYC-related MDM2 contexts was largely precision and screening-quality related rather than evidence against the central CDKN2A-loss MDM2 association.\n\nThe negative findings are important and largely consistent with marker specificity rather than simple driver-gene matching. KRAS mutation is not associated with KRAS dependency, R1 signed +0.014 [-0.004,0.031]; BRAF V600E is not associated with BRAF dependency, R2 -0.017 [-0.045,0.012]; EGFR amplification is not associated with EGFR dependency in discovery or validation, R3 +0.025 [-0.0003,0.051] and R13 -0.022 [-0.061,0.017]; ERBB2 amplification is not associated with ERBB2 dependency, R4 +0.001 [-0.027,0.030]; KRAS mutation is not associated with RIT1 dependency, R5 -0.004 [-0.022,0.015]. Specificity panels support the accepted markers rather than broad non-specific effects: TP53 loss is associated with USP7 but not with the tested matched or broad dependencies; PTEN loss is associated with STAT3 but not with the tested matched or broad dependencies; KEAP1 loss is associated with NFE2L2 but not with USP7 or SMARCA2 in the corresponding tests. Research markers D, E, and F, which were constructed assays with no assigned gene or pathway role, showed no meaningful main or interaction effects. Many technical and context interactions are null, including screen-batch, screen-quality, CRISPR-library, growth-rate, mutation-burden, Cas9-activity, lineage-subtype, and MYC-expression interactions for the largest effects; for example, H241 R233 MDM2 screen-quality interaction +0.061 [-0.015,0.138], H174 R164 MDM2 MYC-expression interaction -0.000 [-0.070,0.069], H175 R165 STAT3 MYC-expression interaction +0.031 [-0.074,0.135], H240 R239 STAT3 PIK3CA interaction +0.001 [-0.150,0.152], and H248 R240 NFE2L2 MYC-expression interaction +0.033 [-0.014,0.081]. These nulls support robustness of the accepted main associations across measured contexts, while also acknowledging that they do not prove absence of all possible effect modification.\n\nSeveral questions remain unresolved because of limited sample size, wide validation intervals, insufficient cells, or deferred testing. The MDM2 CDKN2A contrast in TP53-loss lines H100 R105 +0.083 [-0.018,0.183] and in MYC-amplified lines H170 R155 +0.112 [-0.022,0.246] have positive point estimates but validation intervals crossing zero, so those context-specific claims remain unresolved. The lower-screen-ROC MDM2 CDKN2A estimate H219 R214 +0.071 [0.006,0.136] is small and borderline. WRN MSI-high cannot be evaluated in low mutation-burden lines because the exposed cell is empty, H205 R200 insufficient_cell_n. STAT3 PTEN-loss dependency in non-Avana screens H246 R238 +0.092 [-0.062,0.246] is underpowered and remains library-specific uncertainty, while the overall STAT3 PTEN-loss association remains supported in the main and Avana datasets. Deferred or untested high-value contexts include adenocarcinoma-restricted SMARCA2/SMARCA4 loss, USP7/TP53 loss excluding KEAP1 loss, NFE2L2/KEAP1 loss excluding TP53 loss, SMARCA2/SMARCA4 loss excluding TP53 and KEAP1 loss, adenocarcinoma-restricted NFE2L2/KEAP1 loss, non-Avana SMARCA2/SMARCA4 loss, high-screen-quality NFE2L2/KEAP1 loss, and the remaining active interaction/refinement panel including H236 USP7 TP53 loss by MYC expression, H237 NFE2L2 KEAP1 loss by EMT, H238 SMARCA2 SMARCA4 loss by ASCL2, H239 WRN MSI-high by SLFN11, H247 USP7 TP53 loss by PTEN loss, H249 SMARCA2 SMARCA4 loss by PTEN loss, H250 STAT3 PTEN loss by MYC expression, H251 MDM2 CDKN2A loss by aneuploidy, and H252 WRN MSI-high by EMT. Interactions should be accepted only when the signed interaction interval excludes zero and the magnitude is meaningful relative to the dependency-score scale and the practical threshold; intervals crossing zero are treated as absence of evidence, not proof of equality. The next most informative analysis is therefore to allocate the remaining discovery tests to the active interaction and robustness panel, prioritizing high-power contexts and avoiding underpowered split tests. Overall, the evidence supports dataset-specific marker-dependency associations rather than causal mechanisms or generalizable claims; all marker states are observed nonrandomly, may co-occur with broader genomic or screening context, and the dataset remains restricted to the supplied lung lineage and CRISPR-screening setting.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 19 synthesis. No due assessments and no validation budget remain. Accepted core remains USP7 weaker with TP53 loss; NFE2L2 weaker with KEAP1 loss; SMARCA2 stronger with SMARCA4 loss; WRN stronger with MSI-high; STAT3 stronger with PTEN loss; MDM2 stronger with CDKN2A loss. MDM2 CDKN2A robustness strengthened by H234/R229, H253/R230, H235/R231, H254/R232, H242/R234, H243/R235, H244/R236. STAT3 PTEN robust in Avana H245/R237, unresolved non-Avana H246/R238. Main negatives: driver-matching nulls, research marker D/E/F nulls, many technical/context null interactions. Unresolved: H100, H170, H219, H205, deferred high-value contexts. Next analysis: prioritize active H236-H239, H247, H249-H252 and any deferred tests with adequate cells; accept interactions only if signed CI excludes zero and magnitude meaningful. No causal or generalizability claims."
