igh by high SLFN11 expression gives +0.061 [0.002, 0.119]. It points in the expected direction and the lower bound is just above zero, but the point estimate represents a small modification relative to the large WRN/MSI main effect, the lower bound is close to no effect, and there is substantial multiplicity with small exposed cells in the interaction cells. I therefore leave H239 unresolved rather than accept a borderline effect-modification claim, and close it because the validation budget is exhausted and I do not want to overinterpret this single borderline test.\n\nFrom a critical-review perspective, these tests use measured predictors and QC variables rather than outcome-derived selection, so direct leakage is not apparent, and all valid cells meet the minimum-size diagnostic. However, marker states and expression categories are observational and correlated with broader genomic instability, mutation burden, lineage, growth rate, and screening context; therefore accepted context results remain associations in this dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability. The null interactions are mostly underpowered or precise enough to exclude only large modification, not all possible modification. The accepted context claims strengthen the robustness of the SMARCA2/SMARCA4 and MDM2/CDKN2A associations, while the interaction panel mostly supports marker-context stability rather than strong biological effect modification. No validation is requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
