LFN11 than in low SLFN11, supporting a possible gradient, but the formal interaction is not strong enough to accept as a supported claim. Some low screen-quality or small non-Avana contexts for MDM2 or STAT3 remain unresolved because intervals include zero or lower bounds are too close to the magnitude threshold. The MDM2/CDKN2A-loss association in TP53-loss and MYC-amplification subgroups is also not fully settled because validation intervals cross zero in those narrower subgroups. These should be read as limited evidence in those contexts, not as context independence or rejection of the main MDM2 association.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is to complete the focused context panel, prioritizing the new top-quartile SLFN11 interaction refinement together with the already active H274/H275 full-population SLFN11 tests. If slots remain, proceed through the remaining active aneuploidy, hypoxia, EMT, and MYC context checks. For these later analyses, accept a context effect only if the signed interval excludes zero and the magnitude is meaningful on the dependency-score scale; intervals crossing zero should be interpreted as absence of evidence in that measured context, not as proof that the context does not matter. All conclusions remain observational, dataset-specific associations among measured predictors and CRISPR dependency scores; they do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability beyond these lung-lineage screens.",
