ext, +0.778 [0.737, 0.818]. H259/R309 tests PTEN-loss effects on STAT3 dependency under high aneuploidy, +0.219 [0.114, 0.323]. H260/R310 tests SMARCA4-loss effects on SMARCA2 under high aneuploidy, +0.755 [0.714, 0.795]. H261/R311 tests KEAP1-loss effects on NFE2L2 dependency under high hypoxia, +0.754 [0.711, 0.797]. These are all interval-separated, scientifically meaningful on the dependency-score scale, and consistent with the established marker-dependency associations; I accept them as context-specific observational robustness evidence and close them. H307/R312 tests whether MYC amplification is associated with stronger DHX9 dependency among high-MYC-expression screens. The signed estimate is negative, -0.018 [-0.050, 0.015], and crosses zero, so it does not support the hypothesis; I reject and close it. H276 remains an unresolved deferred interaction, but because this is the final iteration and the direct high- and low-EMT stratum results plus prior EMT-interaction nulls make further analysis uninformative, I close it as unresolved rather than leave active investigation open. No validation can be requested because the validation budget is exhausted. All accepted claims remain dataset-specific associations among measured variables in this lung-lineage CRISPR screen, not causal or mechanistic claims.",
